         "html_value": [
            {
               "text": "<p><hr /></p><p><h3>The Origin of Life</h3>The Biological Sciences, as well as Physics and Chemistry (<htcite0>; <htcite1>), transcend the boundaries of planet Earth. When studying the birth of galaxies, for example, we can identify chemical elements that are essential for life (<htcite2>).</p><p>Like any science, Biology is also directly connected to the language of mathematics. For this reason, we begin this section with Chapter 6 of the <i>First Steps</i>, part, dedicated to the study of mathematics in connection with other sciences. Thus, we recommend reading the first five chapters of that part before proceeding (<htcite3>).</p><p>Although in school we are introduced to subjects called Science or Biology before entering university, teaching often limits itself to presenting only the initial stages of this field. These stages could be referred to as proto-Biology or pre-Biology, as proposed by Dr. Francisco González A. Redondo (<htcite4>; <htcite5>; <htcite6>; <htcite7>).</p></p>In the texts of this section, we present the concepts of pre-Biology and proto-Biology, gradually connecting them to Biology through mathematics.</p>",
